<title>FINLAND: Merita details equity downsizing.</title>
<headline>Merita details equity downsizing.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish banking group Merita Oy on Wednesday gave the following details of main reductions in its share portfolio in the first quarter which reduced its total holdings by 2.6 billion markka to 4.3 billion.</p>
<p>It gave the following details on main holdings:</p>
<p>		    March 31 '97   December 31 '96  Change %-pts</p>
<p>Tamro		 6.3		  10.2	     -3.9</p>
<p>Sampo		15.3		  18.5	     -3.2</p>
<p>Huhtamaki	   1.3		   3.5	     -2.2</p>
<p>UPM-Kymmene	 3.1		   4.9	     -1.8</p>
<p>Metra		 3.1		   4.9	     -1.8</p>
<p>Nokia		 1.7		   3.4	     -1.7</p>
<p>Stockmann	   1.9		   3.3	     -1.4</p>
<p>Pohjola	    14.8		  15.9	     -1.1</p>
<p>Merita said its first quarter profit included a 584 million markka gain from equities downsizing.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki Newsroom +358-9-680 50 242, news@reuters.fi</p>
</text>
